  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PADEO local consultant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of the PADEO trajectory in Sudan. PADEO (Programmatic Approach Sustainable Economic Development) is a pilot program from the Dutch government with a focus on applying a new systematic approach to achieving progress on SDG 8. This new approach encompasses understanding &#x201c;the system&#x201d; the project partners want to operate in and its gaps, knowing the local needs, finding synergies and cooperation with other (local) actors and knowing what the Dutch added value can be.The system that has been chosen to work in is the agribusiness sector in Sudan, and the main challenge to address is to increase the sustainable productivity of the sector.The goal of this project is to 1.	Gain insights in the agribusiness sector in Sudan, specifically to have a better understanding of the local stakeholders, the root causes of the persistent challenges that hinder sustainable productivity, and possible opportunities to improve the sustainable productivity of the agribusiness sector. 2.	Co-create a PADEO program design that positively impacts the sustainable productivity in the agribusiness sector in Sudan, based on insights from local workshops in which the key local stakeholders, including the unusual suspects, have been actively engaged.</narrative>
  </description>
